WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.220
So when I was about, I guess a teenager,
probably

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:10.160
about 13, I decided I need to start
investigating

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:15.200
these things for myself, finding out, you
know, where is this history,

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.200
why doesn't it

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.320
appear anywhere, why isn't it in school,
why isn't it on TV, why

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.000
doesn't I want to talk

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:21.280
about it.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:26.360
I just began to find books and go to, you

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:27.340
know, Canterbury.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:31.640
I think it was a bookshop, you know, you
know, a bookshop linked

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:32.380
to the university.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:37.860
So I could just go and look for books.
Anything, anything related

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:38.700
to Africa,

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:43.940
it could be a novel, it could be history,
it could be anything, all

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:45.680
related to maybe

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:50.840
be African -American and history. I just
buy them and start investigating

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:51.880
and kind of

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:56.940
finding evidence, you know, to combat or
to deal with,

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:57.740
you know, the kind of

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:04.480
world as it affected me. So that's really
where it started. Just

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:07.620
investigating, finding out things for
myself. And then I decided

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:08.460
again at quite

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:13.460
the early age that, you know, wouldn't it
be great to go to university

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:14.340
and study

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:19.500
do these things, this history, and then to
become a school teacher,

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:20.560
I could teach other

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:23.940
people so that they wouldn't have to go
through what I'd gone through

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:24.560
and so on.
